  "text": "A small desktop: three windows, a dock, twelve photographs. Drag a window. It glides, and settles. Every move is worked out by one neural network, built with a library called Handwired. This window shows it, live. Even the wallpaper maps it: one arc for each weight, each number it multiplies by. Nine thousand, nine hundred and nine. Where did those weights come from? Somebody trained it. A tool converted ordinary code. Or it isn't really a network. They hang on this copper line, as paper tags. We'll test every one. And one more tag, blank for now: why would anyone build it this way?",
